[[ch02-introduction]]
== Introduction

What is New Democracy? New Democracy is a new type of Democracy, Mesh Democracy.We are most familiar today with parliamentary or representative democracy. Unlike other types of Democracy, Mesh democracy only has one layer whereas in the US we have Local, State, and Federal layers. If we think of the amount of laws just in the Federal government alone then this book necessarily is limited to ideas not details of laws.



This book is not for academics to debate. It is intended for anyone with a high-school level of education. The plan here and the purpose of this book is for the Entire Planet Earth to adopt New Democracy.

On that note, I'm going to start with a personal story then.

I was mutilated as a baby. I was circumcised. We don't allow parents to pierce ears on babies. You have to be "old enough". But genital mutilation was the norm back in the 1960s. Now, if you had asked my parents why they wanted it done they would have had no answer except that everyone else does it. Neither of my parents graduated high-school and we had no books in our house except the Bible. I grew up in Indiana.

I bring this up because I want to illustrate what adopting New Democracy is up against. We need to understand the cultural forces and head winds preventing any new type of government from being adopted.

Genital mutilation has been around thousands of years. Why? Because it is a tradition. This is how unseen culture propagates for thousands of years. As Christopher Hitchens would say, this is the unthought thought. For thousands of years humans in Western civilization have mutilated genitalia without thought; because everyone else does it.

It is not just that culture is transmitted over thousands of years without thought. We are  also facing wilful ignorance about how culture works. I get frustrated when I hear white people condemn black culture. Why does black culture in America have so much crime? So many kids out of wedlock? Uh, hello, it is because white culture oppresses them. It takes a profound sense of wilful ignorance to not "see" white culture oppressing and killing black people.

So it is not just that culture such as genital mutilation goes on for thousands of years unquestioned, it is that society wilfully doesn't understand the first thing about culture in order to propagate whatever culture they want out of ignorance.

If you join New Democracy this is what we are up against. Heck, the Democratic Socialist party is trying to work within the existing Old Democracy system and those people are being called heretics. New Democracy discards Old Democracy completely.

New Democracy does away with all the following existing culture:

1. Old Democracy
2. Capitalism
3. Nations
4. Rule of law
5. Patriarchy
6. Bureaucracy
7. Hierarchy

That's a lot to take in. But let's do it anyway!

Which came first, the chicken or the egg? Does a working society come before working politics? Yes. A working political system cannot function in a dysfunctional society. Our society is broken, badly. The breakdown of the American family and neighborhood is well documented. I'm only going to provide one piece of intuition here and move on because hundreds of books have been written on this.

Sociologists have observed that the concept of "stranger" no longer exists in Western cultures. Strangers are universally rejected in all cultures. They are a threat to the values, norms, and the stability of a community. The only reason the concept of the stranger no longer matters is that the community is no longer stable. No stable community, no working politics is possible.

In my line of work, software engineering, identifying the root cause is key to success. People incorrectly identify Trump as the root cause. He is not. A broken society is the root cause. You have to at least give credit where credit is due to MAGA. They understand that society has to function first. Of course their idea of fixing society is Christian Nationalism, a nightmare worse than what we have today. But they do understand the task. The left does not. The left completely ignores fixing society. New Democracy is both a solution for society as well as politics. New Democracy builds society first and then builds politics. Only talking about fixing the government is a delusion. MAGA isn't going away, even if they go silent from having failed. MAGA will just rise again if we do not fix society. 

When you think about what this book is proposing as New Democracy with fixing both society and politics then it must be necessarily summary. It also must be necessarily approximate. This is one reason why this is not an academic book. This book is more schematic, or outline, than it is detailed analysis. The hope here is to pique everyone's interest to understand the task at hand: fixing society and then politics.

We can begin New Democracy with just the minimal understanding of what's needed to begin. Primarily everyone needs to join an MGO. This is the social fix. MGOs replace nations as fixed size thirty people. Thirty people can begin to repair their family and the neighborhood. Once an MGO is working then MGOs can form neighborhoods of two-or-three additional MGOs. That's the plan to fix society. After that MGOs coordinate via projects. Projects fix politics.

But, you are not here with the motivation to fix society. Odds are you are here because Trump has induced desperation about politics. So let's talk politics.

What is Democracy? It seems we need to put bookmarks around that before distinguishing old from new. But first, what is the government?

What is the government? Well, simply stated government is a set of laws for society. The government is also the force used to carry those laws. Taxes, police and what not.

For example, Saddam Hussein was the dictator of Iraq that we deposed in the 2003 "War On Terror". Iraq had social laws and the force to carry out those laws. So, what's the difference between Iraq's government and Democracy?

In a word, power. Arbitrary power. Sometimes we call this autocratic, sometimes dictatorial. In any case there exists arbitrary power that is not bound by any law. Those running the government that have arbitrary power always do so by laws implementing tyranny and oppression. But. They still have laws.

When people claim that Democracy is "rule of law" what they really mean is minimal arbitrary power. Arbitrary power has always existed in the United States. Especially when it comes to wars are foreign affairs.

The Trump era of government has been an escalation of arbitrary power and corruption. So, is the United States still governed by the "rule of law"? Or are we closer to Iraq during Saddam Huseein’s years than Old Democracy of 1789?

Old Democracy can be viewed and defined then as a social organization to limit arbitrary power within any rule-of-law system.

Old Democracy was always undermined by lobbyists. The founders recognized lobbyists as a problem they couldn't resolve and just left it to future generations. Rich people buying politicians is as American as the Declaration of Independence. For example, Thomas Jeffersion owned a newspaper where he hired a polyglot who spoke five languages and printed in as many to spread his propaganda. 

John Adams devised a system of checks and balances in the first constitution ever for the State of Massachusetts. The check is on rich people buying politicians via co-equal branches of government. Historians have pointed out that the US being divided into Federal, State and Local governments as further curtailed total corruption by the rich being lobbyists.

However, the wealth of the rich in 2026 is such that all these limits on lobbying have now been successfully defeated. It is now possible to own all politicians at all levels of government by single individuals.

US Democracy is now collapsing at accelerating rates because once the rich own significant pieces then buying what remains becomes cheaper and cheaper.

New Democracy is a way to defeat the rich. It is a rich-proof system for all time. This is primarily because there is no government to bribe. New Democracy is Mesh Democracy that simply stated is made up of just two components: mesh nodes and projects. Mesh nodes are fixed-size, thirty-people, sovereign, micro governments. Projects are how mesh nodes coordinate and organize as society. If today we were New Democracy there would be 200 million “nations” of size thirty people. Further there would be millions of projects. 

Mesh Society is new. The following Overview sections give insight and intuition as to the motivation of Mesh Democracy. However, if one is at their wits end with current Democracy and ready to just dig in then jump to the Handbook sections.

When talking about fixing democracy today there is a spectrum of a.) electing better politicians, b.) starting a nested parted like the Tea Party and Democratic Socialists, c.) major legal changes such as overturning Citizens United, d.) a new Article V convention of States by red States, and e.) a page one rewrite of the US Constitution. However, New Democracy is none of these things. New Democracy is a new system called Mesh Democracy. New Democracy is designed to replace all existing governments on Earth over hundreds of years.

To understand why we need a complete replacement we need to understand the root cause of all failures of all governments worldwide: corruption. This observation about corruption is not new, but centuries old. Quite simply, absolute power corrupts absolutely. A corrarally to that observation is that population size demands more resources, which in turn demands more power, which results in more power and more corruption. What we are seeing today is nothing more complicated than the worldwide population growth equating to runaway corruption worldwide.

Why does absolute power corrupt absolutely? The answer is hierarchy. Hierarchy is the social organization used everywhere. A hierarchy is run by a person or group at the top of a pyramid of people such as kings, CEOs, boards of directors, and so on. Further hierarchies nest. In the US we have Local, State and Federal governments nesting.

Hierarchy doesn't scale. Hierarchy's fundamental flaw is that all power and resources are focused on the top of the pyramid for distribution to those below. The larger the number of people means the more power at the top. The more power equates to more corruption. In Silicon Valley where I worked for decades this is known as your success becomes your failure. This is precisely what happened to the US after WWII. The financial and military success of the US after WWII quickly overran the meager system of checks and balances of the US Constitution. And it wasn't even a fight really. Corruption in the US in 2026 is so large that rewriting the US Constitution would make no difference. I would posit that the only way to fix the US today would be to split the US into fifty different countries, one for each State. Further we would re-apportion States to have no more than ten million population per State. This would dilute the corruption to something pre-WWII. We'd also need to eliminate the US dollar in favor of fifty different dollars, one per new country.

However, re-apportioning the States only kicks the corruption can down the road. Further, it is not just the US where democracy is failing. Democracy is failing worldwide due to the world's increasing population.

Hierarchy is everywhere. Hierarchy defines bureaucracy. Every corporation and every government is built on bureaucracy, that is built on hierarchy. Replacing hierarchy within all of society is a massive undertaking.

The observation that hierarchy doesn't scale means more than just eventually a hierarchy collapses and fails when absolute power becomes too large. The world scale implies that hierarchy is less effective every scale step of the way.

In computer science we scale computers. Networks are designed around orders of magnitude; 10, 100, 1000, 10,000, etc. A design that scales works equally well at each magnitude. Hierarchy degrades as corruption increases at every order of magnitude of size increase. If we are going to replace hierarchy then we need to think about a design that works at every population size, including the entire world population.

But how? Easy, we need to look no further than how computers are networked at scale.

When we think about design for scaling computer networks the term we use is topology, topologies such as a ring topology. In our case we are going to use a mesh topology. In a mesh topology any computer or node can connect with any other computer or node. Further connections are not made using dedicated circuits such as analog telephone calls. Instead connections can involve any number of other nodes and the nodes can change at any time. We call each node connection a hop. A connection can take ten hops one time and three hops another using completely different computers. The number of hops all depends on how busy the nodes are within the mesh topology.

The key to network topology of computers that is relevant to New Democracy is that mesh topologies only grow horizontally. Adding a new computer to a mesh network just adds new capacity for hops to all the nodes in the network. However, vertical paths do exist. We do have vertical mesh connections in the Internet today where ISPs, Internet Service Providers, are the mandatory first hop and typically the mandatory last hop. Technically a router or cable modem is a computer and therefore also a vertical hop.

New Democracy as a mesh design only grows horizontally. That's what is meant by mesh design. Mesh nodes are defined to be fixed size groups of people. These fixed size groups are called micro-governing organizations, or MGOs. These MGOs network via projects. These projects can span from just one up to all the nodes available.

New Democracy as a mesh society design replaces all hierarchy. This includes governments, corporations, and social groups. 

The rest of this book dives deeper into the details of all this. Just realize that the objective is to address the root cause of why all democracies on Earth are failing or degrading: corruption. This corruption is unavoidable for hierarchy. New Democracy eliminates hierarchy. It doesn’t eliminate corruption. It eliminates a system, hierarchy, that always produces corruption. 

The following chapters of this book are divided into two independent sections where each chapter title has the section included:

1. Overview
2. Handbook


The Overview section is in a schematic or sketch format. There are no citations. Partly due to the fact that I'm lazy. I've been working on Irreni since 1980 and haven't kept any notes except my own thoughts. Citations will have to be the effort of other people when the time comes. This is one reason the Overview section addresses just why and motivation. This book then fits within the tradition of Thomas Payne's, "The Rights of Man". Discussing the academic reasons for why and motivation doesn't need to be precise with citations. The objective of the Overview section is to scratch an itch. That itch is curiosity for answers:

1. What is Mesh Democracy?
2. How does it compare to current Democracy?

The Handbook section is what one would expect, how to do this-and-that. Irreni Society is a social engineering project. It is not an ideology project.  As engineering then various parts and pieces can be used independent of the whole. Even if one disagrees with much of the design and engineering of Irreni, then one can still create something new and better using various parts one finds agreeable.

My first handbook was a book of Math tables. I'm old enough to have used slide rulers. However, slide rules were not stand-alone technology. Math handbooks with tables of precalculated commonly used numbers existed long before the slide rule. I used this until Sophomore year in high school. Then I bought a scientific calculator from HP.

My next handbook was, "The Runner's Handbook". This book still exists and has advice for day-to-day training, marathon training, common injuries, and so on.

The Handbook section is in the spirit of these kinds of handbooks but not in body. The  Handbook section is a handbook of quests with suggestions on going about them. You are adventurer going on a quest. One is going on a quest like with Frodo taking the ring to Mount Doom. The initial quest is to find fellow adventurers needed, thirty people to form an Mesh Governing Organization, or MGO. The MGO is the mesh node in Mesh Democracy. How one accomplishes the quest is up to the adventurer where suggestions are given. The Handbook continues assigning finer grained quests with suggestions. The quests are all in support of establishing the MGO.

The Handbook section omits projects. Projects are how two-or-more MGOs coordinate to engineer projects greater than the capabilities of a single MGO. If one is curious about projects there are explanations in the Overview section.

Projects are not included in the Handbook section because forming an MGO will take years. Currently real estate is built as single-family dwellings or apartments. We need new real estate built for thirty people. Further the campus needs new buildings such as a medical bay, dental bay, stores for a year's supply of food and water, and manufacturing. These campuses do not exist today. Therefore the initial generation will focus on getting MGO campuses off the ground.

The two sections combined give an introduction to New Democracy as both reasoning and action. The book chapters are designed to be self contained with minimal dependency on each other. New Democracy is not an ideology with concepts that fits together like a jigsaw puzzle to create a picture. New Democracy is social engineering better represented as an automobile. An automobile has engineering parts such as the wheel that date back to pre-historic years. An automobile can also have engineering from today that is still being developed such as self-driving. An automobile is not an ideology. It is made up of many pieces of engineering to provide function. New Democracy is made up of many pieces of engineering to provide function.

New Democracy as engineering means that it can be broken down and re-assembled into something different. What matters is how New Democracy performs as engineering.

This is why the Handbook sections are quests and not specific recipes. New Democracy is designed for everyone on Earth to be apart of the same organization. New Democracy supports ten-billion people. Different places on Earth are going to require different automobile designs.

New Democracy is not a legal system. A legal system springs from an ideology such as justice. New Democracy as engineering springs from function. New Democracy depends on the Internet. New Democracy also depends on voting. New Democracy does not depend on any one set of functions to be New Democracy. That's what defines ideology. 

The best way to approach New Democracy and this book is like your favorite food buffet. There are lots of plates to choose from and it takes many, many trips back to the restaurant to sample all the dishes. New Democracy is the best kind of buffet where new dishes are created every time one visits.

Old Democracy is founded on ideology. New Democracy is founded on engineering. Just that fact alone means that grasping the concepts will take everyone a hot minute to adjust their thinking. So, best to read this book as parts rather than in one go. Or multiple goes rather than one go.

And finally, enjoy!
